  "body": "This extends PR #13's actual compiled Go path to a finite Parent → Child → Grandchild lifecycle plus an independent Sibling. Go owns request generations, identity, counters, subtree removal/remount and ordered cancellation. React and standalone DOM render the same compiled application contract.\n\nThe shared host now supports an explicit closed effect policy, correlation retirement and typed GoScript effect-slice normalization through the existing generated encoder and Update result TypeID. Ordinary Go `append` remains in application code. Default effect validation stays strict. A reentrant-unmount wrapper bug and a clean-checkout test dependency were repaired with independent reviews.\n\nStacked on `codex/gobi-compiled-methods-20261031` at `6b49cc0bd4c9512a041f723c86b632ec506afd9d`. Current published source `00da54ad0f5a4006b13a5cded18ce291845978bc`, tree `51b64a89b5f7e0edd4792becbed9adad6a27a698`, direct parent `49cc2b96c8817a47319d5b7bd484184a22fa984b`. That parent retains the initial milestone checkpoint (tree `d49ca35b7eda23837c392bbe0d2363551e4c7bec`). The follow-up changes only the conformance executable resolver and four subprocess regression tests.\n\n### Executed so far\n\n- Fresh **explicit partial** `bash run-compiled-lifecycle.sh --lifecycle-only`: 18 commands, 13 stages, 122 stable source pins, zero failures; both real CLI builds produced 67 files with identical AppIR/encoder and separately pinned raw bundles.\n- Native Go, direct emitted module, mounted React, DOM and alternating profiles matched: 26 ticks, 16 clicks, 17 swaps, seven requests, three Grandchild→Child→Parent cancellations, 18 retained detached-button probes, and eight detected mutation controls. Sixteen swaps had callback witnesses (32 fences); one fixed swap checks root/state/pending preservation without a fabricated callback.\n- Final HTTP demo passed; actual Go state, tree, requests/cancellation, sibling survival, remounts, duplicate replies, disabled controls and backend switches are inspectable. No browser errors or WASM.\n- Root independently ran 47 targeted Node tests and both native Go test packages successfully. Typed-effect, unmount, oracle metadata and explicit fresh-appDir repairs have separate preserved findings and acceptance receipts.\n- The separately completed full inherited child passed 17 commands. Hosted evidence confirms Milestone0's 5,000 cases (seed20261030), matching EXPECTED receipt and signed checksums, with all59 executable rule rows intact. The original receipts are preserved.\n\n### Full acceptance is blocked on a reproduced command-path bug\n\nThis remains a **draft**. [Primary push CI 41178420647](https://github.com/samuelpmahan/gondola/actions/runs/41178420647) failed: the conformance CLI resolved bare `--native-go go` into a nonexistent `<checkout>/go`. Source pins were stable. The fresh inherited chain, both compiled builds, runtime suites, direct execution, three browser profiles and 12-check HTTP demo completed, but the final matrix comparison was correctly withheld because its native replay did not execute. The failed provider artifact is retained (ID13034915662, 47,035,803 bytes, SHA256 `6fa057edf26af20b3e6ef805458c92033e2e626d625f44a88bffcc04781762c4`).\n\nThe failure was reproduced locally before editing. The independently accepted repair preserves bare PATH command names, explicit executable paths and the environment default, including invocation from another working directory. Four subprocess tests passed; the final forced-PATH lifecycle-only attempt passed all13stages/18commands with123stable source pins,71pre-build tests,10compiled-runtime checks, complete26-tick/17-swap matrix and12-check HTTP demo. Independent review reran the4tests and matrix, detecting all8mutationcontrols. A new set of28CI workflows is now running on00da54a: [primary push](https://github.com/samuelpmahan/gondola/actions/runs/41181505234), [primary PR](https://github.com/samuelpmahan/gondola/actions/runs/41181508994). No complete current-head hosted pass is claimed.\n\nThe original invalidated local full parent remains failed; its inherited child passed independently. The explicit lifecycle-only pass above remains a separate partial result. [Pending evidence checkpoint](https://github.com/samuelpmahan/gondola/blob/7825f5ff94ac3c96a3fbd1297db19575dd12430f/compiled-lifecycle/ci/2026-10-31/README.md) retains raw attempts, fixes, commands/versions and independent receipts. Its hosted status is explicitly pending; the complete hosted artifact and final acceptance will be published separately. Six actual concurrent Luna6 XHigh workers filled all six available worker slots; native Rebalancer1.0.4 allocations and actual model deliveries are recorded separately. No solver-to-model dispatch is implied.\n\n[Reproduction](https://github.com/samuelpmahan/gondola/blob/49cc2b96c8817a47319d5b7bd484184a22fa984b/compiled-lifecycle/README.md) · [bounded contract](https://github.com/samuelpmahan/gondola/blob/49cc2b96c8817a47319d5b7bd484184a22fa984b/compiled-lifecycle/CONTRACT.md) · [fixed script](https://github.com/samuelpmahan/gondola/blob/49cc2b96c8817a47319d5b7bd484184a22fa984b/compiled-lifecycle/FIXTURE.md).\n\nScope: finite value-owned slots and a deterministic manual effect host, not arbitrary pointer-based Manager compilation or dynamic child graphs. AppIR v1's request/reply capability is coarse; another backend must explicitly implement the closed lifecycle effect profile, typed encoding and cancellation/callback protocol, then pass the same matrix. Other browser engines, IME, hydration, concurrent React, pixels and real network transport remain untested. No main merge or deployment.",
